            <div xml:id="d786">

                <pb facs="0999" n="897" xml:id="pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2974: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-07T11:00:00+01:00">December 7,
                            1935—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 9—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>641. The Secretariat has circulated a telegram dated December 6 from the Emperor
                    of Abyssinia protesting against indiscriminate Italian air bombardments. The
                    Emperor stated that the bombardment of Dessie on December 6 “was established by
                    four Red Cross doctors namely Doctors Dassius, Loeb, Schuppler and Bellot and by
                    the representatives of the Associated Press, the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Times</hi>, Reuter, <hi rendition="#italic">Chicago Tribune</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Daily Express”</hi> He added, “We have ourselves
                    established the death of a tourist and of two children; and the American
                    Hospital of Dessie, which carries with authorization the markings of the Red
                    Cross, has been seriously damaged.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
